Subject: [PATCH 10605/11362] An honest artifact was quarantined today because
 model names are its data

exp6840 (residual-memory chronological shard A) carries flagged_adversarial with a
CRITICAL DURATION_TOO_SHORT. It is honest: six of six acceptance checks passed, the
verdict is an honest null, and the declared substrate is a deterministic CPU
chronological comparison for which 0.038s is plausible.

The cause is that _has_compute_bound_marker scans the whole blob. This experiment's
SUBJECT is model families, so the names appear as row labels and event identifiers
-- "family": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF" and event ids built from the same
strings. Four markers matched, the artifact was classified compute-bound, and the
60s live-model floor was applied. The scan cannot tell "I ran this model" from
"this model name is a value in my dataset".

The harm is present rather than theoretical. The fabrication gate requires capstones
and headline aggregation to skip flagged artifacts, so an honest result with six
passing checks is excluded from this milestone's aggregation and the task logged
FLAGGED instead of OK.

This is the same disease as tonight's REQ-VERIFY-6802 fix, in the half that fix did
not touch. That change added a compute-claim clause and deliberately restricted it
to self-describing fields, because a retrospective that LISTS a training run is not
one -- a whole-blob version made 13 retros compute-bound. The identical argument
applies to the original marker list, which remains whole-blob. Checked directly that
the new clause is not the cause here: the marker function returns True both before
and after that commit, and the identity clause does not fire on this artifact.

The entry gives a population of 222 of 7,078 and labels it an upper bound on where
the mechanism COULD misfire, not a defect count. The heuristic behind it checks six
declaration field names and will miss others, and several members are honestly
blocked runs where nothing executed. Only exp6840 is confirmed, by tracing each
matched string to its position in the data.

Same root cause as the substrate-string gap filed at 05:38Z, in the opposite
direction: there an unrecognised substrate got NO floor and a 3.5ms compute claim
passed; here an unrecognised substrate plus a data-borne marker got the strictest
floor and quarantined honest work.

Not fixed. Requiring the marker in a declaration field rather than anywhere in the
blob would mirror what REQ-VERIFY-6802 did for its own clause, but it inverts which
artifacts face the duration floor corpus-wide and needs a measured A/B first --
the standard the earlier change was held to. Retracting exp6840's stamp through the
sanctioned cleared-note route is an operator decision.

